# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to .npmrc and fill in. .npmrc IS GITIGNORED — never commit a token.
#
#   cp .npmrc.example .npmrc
#
# The token itself is NOT written here. It is read from the environment, so the
# file you create stays safe on disk and safe to have on screen:
#
#   PowerShell   $env:GITHUB_TOKEN = "ghp_..."      (this shell only)
#                setx GITHUB_TOKEN "ghp_..."         (permanent, reopen shell)
#   bash         export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...
#
# Scopes the token needs:
#   read:packages    to INSTALL @tarun1515/jp-shared  — every app needs this
#   (write:packages is only needed in jp-shared, to publish)
#
# Create one at https://github.com/settings/tokens (classic).
#
# ⚠️ If npm reports 404 for @tarun1515/jp-shared, this file or the environment
# variable is the cause nine times out of ten. GitHub Packages answers an
# unauthenticated request for a private package with 404 rather than 401, so
# "not found" almost always means "not authorised".
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

@tarun1515:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
